ivity and in which tooth retention occurs without evidence of any obvious mechanical interference. Instead, malfunction of the eruptive mechanism itself appears to cause nonankylosed permanent teeth to fail to erupt, although the eruption pathway has been cleared by bone resorption. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19061984}. Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.
