P24723	reviewed	PRKCH	Protein kinase C eta type (EC 2.7.11.13) (PKC-L) (nPKC-eta)			DISEASE: Ischemic stroke (ISCHSTR) [MIM:601367]: A stroke is an acute neurologic event leading to death of neural tissue of the brain and resulting in loss of motor, sensory and/or cognitive function. Ischemic strokes, resulting from vascular occlusion, is considered to be a highly complex disease consisting of a group of heterogeneous disorders with multiple genetic and environmental risk factors. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:17206144}. Note=Disease susceptibility is associated with variations affecting the gene represented in this entry.
