O00255	reviewed	MEN1	Menin		99879;97279;652;314790;2965;314786;	DISEASE: Familial multiple endocrine neoplasia type I (MEN1) [MIM:131100]: Autosomal dominant disorder characterized by tumors of the parathyroid glands, gastro-intestinal endocrine tissue, the anterior pituitary and other tissues. Cutaneous lesions and nervous-tissue tumors can exist. Prognosis in MEN1 patients is related to hormonal hypersecretion by tumors, such as hypergastrinemia causing severe peptic ulcer disease (Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, ZES), primary hyperparathyroidism, and acute forms of hyperinsulinemia. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10090472, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10229909, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10534569, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10576763, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10617276, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10660339, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10664520, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10849016, ECO:0000269|PubMed:10993647, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11102994, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11134142, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11241849, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12050235, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12112656, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12417605, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12652570, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12699448, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12746426, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12791038, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14686752, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14992727, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15714081, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15730416, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17555499, ECO:0000269|PubMed:22327296, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9103196, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9215689, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9215690, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9463336, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9506756, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9671267, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9683585, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9709921, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9709976, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9709985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9740255, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9747036, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9820618, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9832038, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9888389, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9989505}. Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.; DISEASE: Note=MEN1 inactivating mutations are responsible for hyperfunctioning of the parathyroid glands and subsequent primary hyperparathyroidism. 